<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of Schleswig-Holstein</h1><p class="st-meta">1848 CE – 1851 CE · capital Kiel</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Rebel German government set up in Kiel in 1848 to free Schleswig and Holstein from Denmark, which fought the First Schleswig War and lost.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In March 1848, as revolutions spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark's</a> new liberal government moved to tie <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> more closely to the kingdom. German nationalists in the duchies responded by forming a provisional government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiel">Kiel</a> on 24 March, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-hartwig-beseler">Wilhelm Hartwig Beseler</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-frederick-of-noer">Prince Frederick of Noer</a>, claiming both duchies for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government raised a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a> army and received support from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a>, whose troops fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> in 1848-1849. It governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiel">Kiel</a> with the backing of the German-speaking estates, while Danish-minded inhabitants of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> opposed it. Great-power pressure forced Prussia to make peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in 1850.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Fighting alone, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a> army was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-isted">Isted</a> (Idstedt) in July 1850. Under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, the government dissolved in early 1851, and Danish rule was restored. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> Protocol of 1852 confirmed the settlement, but the dispute reignited in the war of 1864.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1848 CE – 1851 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.48%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1848 CE – 1851 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kiel</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wilhelm Hartwig Beseler, Prince Frederick of Noer</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Germany, Denmark</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Schleswig-Holstein (1848-1851), Provisorische Regierung</dd></dl></aside></div>
